From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Badis Meddouri <meddouri.badis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 02:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: log the LE HID path (release builds are silent)

APPL_TRACE_DEBUG is gated behind appl_trace_level >= BT_TRACE_LEVEL_DEBUG, so
in a release build the entire LE HID-over-GATT path logs nothing when it fails.
Add LOG_INFO lines at the three points that matter: the GATT open request, the
GATT open result, and the security/encryption branch.

This is what identified the actual failure:

  [karat-hid] le_open_conn bda=84:28:59:07:a1:6e gatt_if=3 transport=DIRECT_CONNECT
  [karat-hid] gatt_open bda=84:28:59:07:a1:6e status=133 (FAILED) conn_id=0
  bta_gattc_open_fail: Cannot establish Connection. Return GATT_ERROR(133)
  acl_ble_connection_fail: hci_status:Connection Accept Timeout

status=133 is GATT_ERROR (0x85) and "Connection Accept Timeout" is HCI 0x08: the
remote does not accept an incoming LE connection at all. HID discovery and the
security step are never reached. Purely diagnostic, no behaviour change.

--- a/packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/bta/hh/bta_hh_le.cc
+++ b/packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/bta/hh/bta_hh_le.cc
@@ -274,6 +274,9 @@ void bta_hh_le_open_conn(tBTA_HH_DEV_CB* p_cb, const RawAddress& remote_bda) {
   bta_hh_cb.le_cb_index[BTA_HH_GET_LE_CB_IDX(p_cb->hid_handle)] = p_cb->index;
   p_cb->in_use = true;
 
+  /* karat: see bta_hh_gatt_open() - the LE path logs nothing in a release build. */
+  LOG_INFO("[karat-hid] le_open_conn bda=%s gatt_if=%d transport=DIRECT_CONNECT",
+           remote_bda.ToString().c_str(), bta_hh_cb.gatt_if);
   BTA_GATTC_Open(bta_hh_cb.gatt_if, remote_bda, BTM_BLE_DIRECT_CONNECTION,
                  false);
 }
